From 2399c44fd4496342b7a153f6d1f48ed140abd2c7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 01:12:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 14/21] feat(matcher): the two no-name cards, and the
 connection on both yes (1699 part 2, A16)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

D679/D680. Part 1 proposes matches (a need × an offer in the same field).
Now they reach people. All of it is server text; no model text.

- At 08:00 UTC (noon in Tbilisi, so nobody is woken by a match) card 1 goes
  to the need's owner in his goal's conversation, with one push: „Someone in
  your circle is open to exactly this — <field>. Shall I ask whether they
  want to talk?" yes / no. One match card per person per day.
- His yes: card 2 goes to the offer's owner, naming only the field and never
  the goal's words: „Someone in your circle needs something in your field —
  <field>. Shall I put you in touch?"
- Her yes: both are named to each other. He is told what to pass on and that
  Netai carries it (D438); she is told he will write through Netai.
- A no on either side closes it. He hears „Nothing came of it this time."
  only if he had already said yes. Matches expire after 14 days, with the
  same rule.
Migration 226 records where each card was shown, so a tap finds its match.
Offers are empty until §109, so nothing goes out before Misho's yes.

DONE WHEN (after §109): seat A's goal „investor for a hotel" × seat B's offer
„hotel / hospitality" (same field word); after 08:00 UTC A gets card 1 with no
name; A taps yes; B gets card 2 with no name and no goal text; B taps yes;
both are named; a no on either side closes it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
